 gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.14), gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), gir1.2-glib-2.0, bluez
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator, pulseaudio-utils
Description: settings for HUAWEI FreeBuds earphones on GNOME
 Sirène sets HUAWEI FreeBuds earphones (6i, 7i, 4i) from the desktop, over
 their own Bluetooth channel: noise cancellation and awareness modes, every
 gesture, equalizer, sound quality priority, low latency, wear detection,
 dual connect, and the battery of each earbud and of the case.
 .
 It pauses the players that were playing when an earbud is taken out, and
 resumes them when it is put back. It waits quietly in the background and
 shows an icon in the top bar while the earphones are connected, with the
 batteries and the noise control; it can also announce Bluetooth connections,
 low batteries and volume changes (with the Custom OSD extension).
 .
 The HUAWEI protocol comes from OpenFreebuds.
